    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0fd994c5_b7898c0f",
        "filename": "common/base32.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-22T00:55:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is this a standard algorithm or is it something you came up with?\n\nalso, how about calculating crc8 over the unencoded stream and only including lower 5 bits in the encoded stream? This way you could use crc8?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "f870a3eb787ecb5feef3853c4c0472643b7a8839",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0bf08d51_25386377",
        "filename": "common/base32.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-22T01:14:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Non-standard, but well-tested for the properties I want (operates a 5-bit symbol at a time, and guarantees detection of any single-symbol typo or two transposed symbols).\n\nWe can\u0027t reuse crc8() anyway, because the stream is not necessarily a whole number of bytes.",
      "parentUuid": "0fd994c5_b7898c0f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "f870a3eb787ecb5feef3853c4c0472643b7a8839",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
